<title>UK: Access Plus shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Access Plus shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Access Plus Plc, a marketing services group, set a premium on their first day of trading on London Stock Exchange on Monday.</p>
<p>By 1405 GMT the shares were marked up at 107-1/2p, although no trade was registered in the stock.</p>
<p>The shares were placed at 90p, valuing Access Plus at 12.6 million stg. The company said it planned to grow by increasing sales, expanding its product range and making acquisitions.</p>
<p>The nominated adviser was Brown Shipley &amp; Co and the nominated broker was Rowan Dartington &amp; Co.</p>
<p>-- John Sutherland, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7945</p>
